   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 2c, $L=3$ [hp 70 digits]:** the Q-form with the norm from the eigenvector equals the direct $|C|$ to $\\sim10^{-41}$ at every $\\varepsilon$ on all six $[1,0,1]$ states (conjugate pairs have equal moduli), and the extrapolated $|C|=0.17112641,\\ 0.027137747,\\ 0.045900846\\,(\\times2),\\ 0.15348408\\,(\\times2)$ equal the data (last-but-one column) to the printed 8 digits. $\\mathbb A$ extrapolates to $3.65685,\\ 7.65685,\\ 14.658,\\ 1.842$, the known $K_1$ values on these states. **Scaling difference to $L=2$:** at $L=3$ the factors are *not* separately finite: $\\mathbb W\\sim\\varepsilon^{2}$ (e.g. $4.9\\cdot10^{-3},\\ 1.2\\cdot10^{-3},\\ 3.0\\cdot10^{-4}$ on the first state), $|\\langle0|\\Psi\\rangle|/\\|\\Psi\\|\\sim\\varepsilon^{-3}$ and $\\mathcal N_{\\rm pre}\\sim\\varepsilon$; only the product is finite. (The last column of the table shows the extrapolated $|\\mathbb W|\\to0$.)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Part 3. The $\\varepsilon\\to0$ limit of $\\mathbb A$ and $\\mathbb W$ at $L=2$ (new)\n\nGoal: express $\\lim_{\\varepsilon\\to0}$ of the two Q-factors by **untwisted** eigenvalue data at the ABJM point $z=1$, $\\theta_F=(0,0)$, $\\theta_A=(1,1)$ ($h=\\tfrac12$, $u_0=\\tfrac12$). The limits are integers on the two singlets, $(\\mathbb A,\\mathbb W)\\to(10,25)$ and $(2,9)$. (The SoV norm $\\mathbb B$ is the known Q-function norm and is outside the scope of this notebook.)\n\n**3.1** exact untwisted singlets and their pair eigenvalue data; **3.2** $\\mathbb A\\to K_1=2-A-B-C$; **3.3** $\\mathbb W\\to B_1^2$, including the behaviour of the normalised $y_s=\\tau_1(\\theta_s)/\\kappa_s$ as $\\nu=\\theta_{F1}-\\theta_{F2}\\to0$.\n\n### 3.1 Untwisted ABJM chain, $L=2$: exact singlets and their pair eigenvalue data\n\nAll operators are built at the untwisted chain with $G=\\mathbb 1$; the singlets are the two-dimensional joint kernel of the six $su(4)$ raising/lowering generators in the zero-weight sector ($\\dim=28$); they are joint eigenvectors of $t_k(u)$. Data per pair: $\\tau_F=\\tau_1(0)$, $\\tau_F'=\\tau_1'(0)$, $x=\\tau_1(u_0)$, $\\tau_A=\\tau_1(1)$, $\\tau_1'(u_0)$, $\\tau_2(u_0)$, $w=\\tau_2'(u_0)-\\tau_1'(u_0)\\tau_F$, $y=\\tau_3'(u_0)$, $\\tilde w=\\tau_2'(1)-\\tau_A\\tau_1'(u_0)$, $\\tilde y=\\tau_3'(3/2)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 3.1 untwisted ABJM chain, L = 2, G = identity: exact singlets and exact pair data (exact algebraic numbers) *)\nqfUntw = Module[{h = 1/2, ty = qfTy4, th = {1, 0, 1, 0}, I4 = IdentityMatrix[4], Gs, blk, gen, ops, big, nsp, A, T1u, T2u, T3u, T2A, T3A, T10, mm, es, out, M1, sec0 = qfZero},\n  Gs = {I4}; blk[m_] := Normal[m[[sec0, sec0]]];\n  T10 = qfTmulti[1, Gs, 0, ty, th, h, True][[1]]; A = qfTmulti[1, Gs, 1, ty, th, h, False][[1]]; T1u = qfTmulti[1, Gs, 1/2, ty, th, h, True][[1]];\n  T2u = qfTmulti[2, Gs, 1/2, ty, th, h, True][[1]]; T3u = qfTmulti[3, Gs, 1/2, ty, th, h, True][[1]]; T2A = qfTmulti[2, Gs, 1, ty, th, h, True][[1]]; T3A = qfTmulti[3, Gs, 3/2, ty, th, h, True][[1]];\n  gen[i_, j_] := Plus @@ Table[KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[4^(s - 1), SparseArray], If[ty[[s]] === \"A\", SparseArray[{{i, j} -> 1}, {4, 4}], SparseArray[{{j, i} -> -1}, {4, 4}]], IdentityMatrix[4^(4 - s), SparseArray]], {s, 4}];\n  ops = {{1, 2}, {2, 3}, {3, 4}, {2, 1}, {3, 2}, {4, 3}};\n  big = Join @@ Table[Normal[gen @@ p][[All, sec0]], {p, ops}]; nsp = NullSpace[big];\n  M1 = blk[T10[[1]]]; mm = Transpose[Table[LinearSolve[Transpose[nsp], M1 . nsp[[i]]], {i, Length[nsp]}]]; es = Eigensystem[mm];\n  out = Table[Module[{psi = es[[2, m]] . nsp, p, ev},\n     psi = psi/Sqrt[psi . psi]; p = First[Ordering[Abs[psi], -1]]; ev[op_] := Simplify[(blk[op] . psi)[[p]]/psi[[p]]];\n     Module[{tF = ev[T10[[1]]], dF = ev[T10[[2]]], tA = ev[A], x = ev[T1u[[1]]], d1 = ev[T1u[[2]]], t2 = ev[T2u[[1]]], d2 = ev[T2u[[2]]], d3 = ev[T3u[[2]]], d2A = ev[T2A[[2]]], d3A = ev[T3A[[2]]], t3 = ev[T3u[[1]]]},\n      <|\"dim\" -> Length[nsp], \"tauF\" -> tF, \"dtauF\" -> dF, \"tauA\" -> tA, \"x\" -> x, \"d1\" -> d1, \"t2u\" -> t2, \"w\" -> d2 - d1 tF, \"y\" -> d3, \"wt\" -> d2A - tA d1, \"yt\" -> d3A, \"t3u\" -> t3, \"psi\" -> psi|>]], {m, 2}];\n  out];\nqfUntwData = Map[KeyDrop[#, \"psi\"] &, qfUntw];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[Lookup[qfUntwData[[j]], {\"tauF\", \"dtauF\", \"tauA\", \"x\", \"d1\", \"t2u\", \"w\", \"y\", \"wt\", \"yt\", \"t3u\"}], {j, 2}], {\"tau_1(0)\", \"tau_1'(0)\", \"tau_A = tau_1(1)\", \"x = tau_1(1/2)\", \"tau_1'(1/2)\", \"tau_2(1/2)\", \"w\", \"y = tau_3'(1/2)\", \"w~\", \"y~ = tau_3'(3/2)\", \"tau_3(1/2)\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
