   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 3.2 [exact on the untwisted chain; hp on the $\\varepsilon$-chain]:** on the exact singlets the regularised untwisted $\\hat t_3(u_0)$ has eigenvalue $\\mp\\tfrac9{64}$ ($E=4$, $E=20$ respectively), $(A,B,C)=(-2,4,-2)$ and $(2,-12,2)$, $AC=4$, and $K_1=2-A-B-C=2,\\ 10$, equal to the one-pair Q-formula $2-8\\tau-\\frac1{2\\tau}+64x\\tau$; the normalised eigenvalues $A,B,C$ of the twisted $\\varepsilon$-chain (table above) extrapolate to exactly these values, so $P_\\kappa(\\tau_\\varepsilon)\\to K_1(\\tau_0)$ and $\\mathbb A\\to10,\\ 2$ (Part 2). Two points worth recording: (a) the limit is taken with the **normalised** $A,B,C$ (the raw $t_3'(u_0)$ vanishes like $\\nu$, the double zero of the prefactor at $\\nu=0$, and is divided by $\\lambda_3\\propto\\nu$); (b) $AC=4$ is the exact operator statement $\\hat X_3X_1=\\tfrac9{256}P$ (pair translation $P$), so $K_1$ is a function of the two numbers $\\tau_1(\\theta_F),\\tau_1(\\theta_F+h)$ on translation-invariant states.\n\n### 3.3 $\\mathbb W\\to B_1(y)^2$\n\nWrite $\\theta=(\\theta_{F1}+2h,\\theta_{F1},\\theta_{F2}+2h,\\theta_{F2})$, $\\nu=\\theta_{F1}-\\theta_{F2}$, $\\tau_2=\\tau_1(\\theta_{F1})$, $\\tau_4=\\tau_1(\\theta_{F2})$. The explicit $\\kappa$'s are $\\kappa_2=2h^2\\nu(\\nu-2h)$, $\\kappa_4=2h^2\\nu(\\nu+2h)$ and $g=\\nu^2/(\\nu^2-h^2)$, so\n$$y_2=\\frac{\\tau_2}{2h^2\\nu(\\nu-2h)},\\quad y_4=\\frac{\\tau_4}{2h^2\\nu(\\nu+2h)},\\qquad B_z=z^2-z(y_2+y_4)+g\\,y_2y_4 .$$\n**The normalised $y_s$ do not have finite untwisted limits:** $\\nu y_2\\to-\\tau/(4h^3)$, $\\nu y_4\\to+\\tau/(4h^3)$, i.e. $y_{2,4}\\sim\\mp2\\tau/\\nu$ at $h=\\tfrac12$. Only the combinations in $B_z$ are finite: $g\\to-\\nu^2/h^2$ turns $g\\,y_2y_4\\to\\tau^2/(16h^8)$, and in $y_2+y_4$ the poles cancel because $\\tau_2-\\tau_4=\\nu\\,\\tau'+O(\\nu^2)$ with $\\tau'=\\partial_u\\tau_1(u)|_{\\theta_F}$ the eigenvalue of $t_1'(\\theta_F)$ (the $O(\\varepsilon)$ twist shifts of $\\tau$ cancel in this difference):\n$$y_2+y_4\\ \\to\\ -\\frac{\\tau+h\\tau'}{4h^4},\\qquad B_{z_2},B_{z_3}\\to B_1=1+\\frac{\\tau+h\\tau'}{4h^4}+\\frac{\\tau^2}{16h^8}\\overset{h=1/2}{=}1+4\\tau+2\\tau'+16\\tau^2 .$$\nSo $\\mathbb W\\to B_1^2$, a perfect square of a **one-pair** quantity (it involves the single-pair eigenvalue function $\\tau_1(u)$ and its derivative at $\\theta_F$). Because $t_1(u)$ is a degree-4 polynomial in $u$ with leading coefficient $\\mathrm{tr}\\,G=4$ at the untwisted point, and on parity-symmetric states ($\\tau_1(u)=\\tau_1(1-u)$, observed) it is a polynomial in $(u-\\tfrac12)^2$, one has $\\tau'(0)=4x-4\\tau-1$ with $x=\\tau_1(\\tfrac12)$, hence $B_1=16\\tau^2-4\\tau-1+8x$, a function of $\\tau_1(\\theta_F)$ and $\\tau_1(\\theta_F+h)$ only.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 3.3 numerics: poles of y_s, finite combinations, B_1(eps), and the untwisted limit formula on the exact singlets *)\nqfWan = Table[Table[Module[{e = qfEpsL2[[i]], S, h = qfHh, th, thF, z, nu, kS, y2, y4, g, B1, row = qfSingE[[j, i]]},\n    S = qfSetup[e]; th = S[\"th\"]; thF = S[\"thF\"]; z = S[\"z\"]; nu = S[\"nu\"]; kS = Table[qfKappaS[2 q, th, h], {q, 2}]; {y2, y4} = row[\"tauF\"]/kS; g = nu^2/(nu^2 - h^2);\n    {e, N[nu y2, 8], N[nu y4, 8], N[y2 + y4, 8], N[g y2 y4, 8], N[1 - (y2 + y4) + g y2 y4, 8], N[qfBz[z[[2]], {y2, y4}, thF, h], 8], N[qfBz[z[[3]], {y2, y4}, thF, h], 8], N[Sqrt[Abs[row[\"W\"]]], 8]}], {i, 5}], {j, 2}];\nqfWlim = Table[Table[qfExtrapE[qfWan[[j, All, k]]], {k, 2, 9}], {j, 2}];\nqfWuntw = Table[Module[{d = SelectFirst[qfUntwData, #[\"tauF\"] == If[j == 1, 1/4, -1/4] &], tau, dtau, x, B1a, B1b},\n    tau = d[\"tauF\"]; dtau = d[\"dtauF\"]; x = d[\"x\"]; B1a = 1 + 4 tau + 2 dtau + 16 tau^2; B1b = 16 tau^2 - 4 tau - 1 + 8 x;\n    {{\"E = 20\", \"E = 4\"}[[j]], tau, dtau, x, -2 tau, 2 tau, -4 (tau + dtau/2), 16 tau^2, B1a, B1b, 4 x - 4 tau - 1}], {j, 2}];\nColumn[Join[Table[Labeled[Grid[Prepend[Table[Join[{qfEpsL2[[i]]}, qfWan[[j, i]][[2 ;; 9]]], {i, 5}] // Append[#, Join[{\"eps -> 0\"}, N[qfWlim[[j]], 10]]] &, {\"eps\", \"nu y_2\", \"nu y_4\", \"y_2 + y_4\", \"g y_2 y_4\", \"B_1 = 1-(y2+y4)+g y2 y4\", \"B_{z2}(y)\", \"B_{z3}(y)\", \"sqrt|W|\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left], {\"singlet E = 20\", \"singlet E = 4\"}[[j]], Top], {j, 2}],\n  {Labeled[Grid[Prepend[qfWuntw, {\"singlet\", \"tau = tau_1(0)\", \"tau' = tau_1'(0)\", \"x = tau_1(1/2)\", \"limit nu y_2 = -tau/(4h^3)\", \"limit nu y_4\", \"limit y_2+y_4 = -(tau+h tau')/(4h^4)\", \"limit g y_2 y_4 = tau^2/(16 h^8)\", \"B_1 = 1+4tau+2tau'+16tau^2\", \"B_1 = 16 tau^2 - 4 tau - 1 + 8x\", \"tau' (parity) = 4x-4tau-1\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left], \"limit formulas from the exact untwisted singlets (3.1)\", Top]}]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
