n class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:19.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-31.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:19.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-32.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:19.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-33.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:19.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-34.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:19.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-36.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:19.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-37.3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:19.65em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:17.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:18.99em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[128]= \\begin{matrix}\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{\\# states where the deviation halves with eps (ratio 1.8..2.2) and is < 5\\% at eps = 1/1600} & 2\\\\\\hline\\text{of which real} & 2\\\\\\hline\\text{max deviation at eps = 1/1600 among them} & 0.000685\\\\\\hline\\end{array}\\\\\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{state} & \\text{real} & \\text{tau\\_F1 (eps = 1/1600)} & \\text{|W - B1\\^{}2|/|W|, eps = 1/800} & \\text{eps = 1/1600} & \\text{ratio}\\\\\\hline1 & \\mathrm{True} & 0.24991 & 0.00137 & 0.000685 & 2.00\\\\\\hline2 & \\mathrm{False} & 0.\\times 10^{-8}+0.25013\\,\\mathrm{i} & 2.05\\times 10^{6} & 8.22\\times 10^{6} & 0.250\\\\\\hline3 & \\mathrm{False} & 0.\\times 10^{-8}-0.25013\\,\\mathrm{i} & 2.05\\times 10^{6} & 8.22\\times 10^{6} & 0.250\\\\\\hline4 & \\mathrm{True} & -0.25014 & 0.000974 & 0.000487 & 2.00\\\\\\hline5 & \\mathrm{False} & 0.\\times 10^{-8}+0.25011\\,\\mathrm{i} & 1.03\\times 10^{7} & 4.14\\times 10^{7} & 0.250\\\\\\hline6 & \\mathrm{False} & 0.\\times 10^{-8}-0.25011\\,\\mathrm{i} & 1.03\\times 10^{7} & 4.14\\times 10^{7} & 0.250\\\\\\hline7 & \\mathrm{False} & 0.\\times 10^{-8}+0.25002\\,\\mathrm{i} & 121000 & 484000 & 0.250\\\\\\hline8 & \\mathrm{False} & 0.\\times 10^{-8}-0.25002\\,\\mathrm{i} & 121000 & 484000 & 0.250\\\\\\hline… [latex truncated: 2903 chars total]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "2f368aab-4be7-45d1-b383-fc939edefcac"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Check on all 28 zero-weight states.** The parity shortcut $B_1=16\\tau^2-4\\tau-1+8x$ (table above) holds on the two singlets only: on the other states it fails (e.g. the states with $\\tau_F=\\pm i/4$ have $\\mathbb W\\to0$ and $K_1=0$, while the shortcut gives $B_1=\\mp i$), so $\\tau_1'(\\theta_F)$ is genuine extra Q-data in general and the shortcut is not claimed beyond the singlets. The general formula $B_1=1+4\\tau+2\\tau'+16\\tau^2$ is tested next with $\\tau'$ the eigenvalue of $t_1'(\\theta_{F1})$ on the $\\varepsilon$-chain (one more build per $\\varepsilon$), on all 28 states, at $\\varepsilon=1/800$ and $1/1600$: $\\mathbb W(\\varepsilon)-B_1^2(\\tau,\\tau')$ must fall like $\\varepsilon$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 3.3 general formula on all 28 states: W(eps) vs B1^2, B1 = 1 + (tau + h tau')/(4 h^4) + tau^2/(16 h^8), tau' = eigenvalue of t1'(theta_F1) on the eps-chain *)\nqfEvalTp[eps_, prec_] := Module[{S = qfSetup[eps], h = qfHh, Lam, th, ty = qfTy4, thF, z, u0, blk, TD1, F1, D1, F2, T2, T3d, comb, vals, vecs, VR, piv, ev, X1v, F2v, D1v, kapS, rows},\n   Lam = DiagonalMatrix[S[\"z\"]]; th = S[\"th\"]; thF = S[\"thF\"]; z = S[\"z\"]; u0 = thF[[1]] + h; blk[m_] := Normal[m[[qfZero, qfZero]]];\n   TD1 = qfTmulti[1, {Lam}, thF[[1]], ty, th, h, True][[1]]; F1 = blk[TD1[[1]]]; D1 = blk[TD1[[2]]]; F2 = blk[qfTmulti[1, {Lam}, thF[[2]], ty, th, h, False][[1]]];\n   T2 = blk[qfTmulti[2, {Lam}, u0, ty, th, h, False][[1]]]; T3d = blk[qfTmulti[3, {Lam}, u0, ty, th, h, True][[1, 2]]];\n   {vals, vecs} = Eigensystem[N[F1 + 2/5 F2 + 3/7 T2 + 5 T3d, prec]]; VR = Transpose[vecs]; piv = Table[First[Ordering[Abs[VR[[All, n]]], -1]], {n, 28}];\n   ev[op_] := Module[{X = N[op, prec] . VR}, Table[X[[piv[[n]], n]]/VR[[piv[[n]], n]], {n, 28}]];\n   X1v = ev[F1]; F2v = ev[F2]; D1v = ev[D1]; kapS = Table[qfKappaS[2 q, th, h], {q, 2}];\n   Table[Module[{yv = {X1v[[n]], F2v[[n]]}/kapS, Wv, B1},\n     Wv = qfBz[z[[2]], yv, thF, h] qfBz[z[[3]], yv, thF, h]; B1 = 1 + (X1v[[n]] + h D1v[[n]])/(4 h^4) + X1v[[n]]^2/(16 h^8);\n     {n, N[X1v[[n]], 6], N[D1v[[n]], 6], N[Wv, 6], N[B1^2, 6], N[Abs[Wv - B1^2]/(1 + Abs[B1^2]), 3]}], {n, 28}]];\nqfTpRes = {qfEvalTp[1/800, 90], qfEvalTp[1/1600, 100]};\nqfTpTab = Table[Join[qfTpRes[[2, n]], {N[qfTpRes[[1, n, 6]]/Max[qfTpRes[[2, n, 6]], 10^-30], 3]}], {n, 28}];\nColumn[{Grid[{{\"# states with |W - B1^2|/(1+|B1^2|) < 1e-2 at eps = 1/1600\", Count[qfTpTab[[All, 6]], x_ /; x < 10^-2]}, {\"max over all 28 states of the deviation at eps = 1/1600, 1/800\", {Max[qfTpRes[[2, All, 6]]], Max[qfTpRes[[1, All, 6]]]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[qfTpTab, {\"state\", \"tau_1(theta_F1)\", \"tau' = t1'(theta_F1)\", \"W (eps = 1/1600)\", \"B1^2 (formula)\", \"|W - B1^2|/(1+|B1^2|)\", \"ratio of deviations 1/800 : 1/1600\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
