   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Part 4. Summary\n\n**The ABJM $M=1$ even-bridge structure constant in Q-functions, $L=2$ (and tested at $L=3$).**\n$$\\vert C_{M=1}\\vert=\\lim_{\\varepsilon\\to0}\\ \\mathcal N_{\\rm pre}\\;P_\\kappa(\\tau)\\;B_{z_2}(y)B_{z_3}(y)\\;\\frac{\\vert\\langle0\\vert\\Psi\\rangle\\vert}{\\Vert\\Psi\\Vert},\\qquad \\frac{\\vert\\langle0\\vert\\Psi\\rangle\\vert}{\\Vert\\Psi\\Vert}\\simeq\\frac1{\\sqrt{\\mathbb B}}\\ (\\text{known SoV norm}),$$\nwith $\\mathcal N_{\\rm pre}=(a/\\kappa_0)^n(\\lambda_1u_4)^{-L}/(1-\\kappa z_1)^2$ explicit; $P_\\kappa=s^2+\\kappa s(A+B+C)+\\kappa^2AC/4$ built from the single-pair eigenvalues $\\tau_1(\\theta_{F1}),\\tau_2(u_0),\\hat\\tau_3(u_0)$; $B_z(y)=\\sum_S(-z)^{L-\\vert S\\vert}\\prod_{s<t\\in S}\\frac{\\nu_{st}^2}{\\nu_{st}^2-h^2}\\prod_{s\\in S}y_s$ with $y_s=\\tau_1(\\theta_s)/\\kappa_s$.\n\n**Untwisted limits at $L=2$ (Part 3).** $\\mathbb A\\to K_1=2-A-B-C=2-8\\tau-\\frac1{2\\tau}+64x\\tau$ ($\\tau=\\tau_1(\\theta_F)$, $x=\\tau_1(\\theta_F+h)$; $K_1=10,2$ on the singlets); $\\mathbb W\\to B_1^2$, $B_1=1+4\\tau+2\\tau'+16\\tau^2$, $\\tau'=\\partial_u\\tau_1\\vert_{\\theta_F}$ ($\\sqrt{\\mathbb W}=5,3$ on the singlets); the normalised $y_s$ individually diverge like $1/\\nu$ and only the combinations $y_2+y_4$, $g\\,y_2y_4$ are finite. So\n$$\\vert C_{M=1}\\vert=K_1\\,B_1^2\\big/\\sqrt{\\mathbb B_0},\\qquad(\\mathbb A_0,\\mathbb W_0,\\mathbb B_0)=(10,25,2.5\\cdot10^6),\\ (2,9,7776)\\ \\Rightarrow\\ 1/\\sqrt{40},\\ 1/\\sqrt{24}.$$\n\n| statement | where | level |\n|---|---|---|\n| $\\langle W_a^L\\vert K_\\kappa=(1-\\kappa z_1)^2\\langle W_{a'}\\otimes W_a^{L-1}\\vert$ ($z_2=z_3$, ABJM pairs) | 1(a), $L=2$ (python exact at $L=3$ earlier) | exact |\n| for $z_2\\ne z_3$ the identity fails at finite twist and holds only as $\\varepsilon\\to0$ | 1(a) control, 2a | exact (residual 0.069) / hp |\n| $\\langle0_w\\vert\\Psi\\rangle=(v_1u_4)^L\\langle W_a^L\\vert\\Psi\\rangle$ and the Möbius map | 1(b), all five sectors, $L=2$ | hp 40 digits; Möbius map exact (symbolic) |\n| $B_{z_2}B_{z_3}$ Q-form of $\\langle W_a\\vert\\Psi\\rangle/\\langle0\\vert\\Psi\\rangle$ | 1(c): $L=2$ (108 states, two $\\theta$); $L=3$ ($n=0,1,2$, 7 states) | hp 50 digits ($<10^{-41}$); general-$L$ proof open |\n| $\\vert C\\vert\\to1/\\sqrt{40},1/\\sqrt{24}$ from $\\mathcal N_{\\rm pre}\\mathbb A\\mathbb W\\vert\\langle0\\vert\\Psi\\rangle\\vert/\\Vert\\Psi\\Vert$ | 2a, $L=2$, $\\varepsilon=1/100..1/1600$ | hp 90-110 digits, extrapolation $\\sim10^{-15}$ |\n| $\\mathbb B=\\sum\\tilde\\tau M\\tau$ equals the SoV pairing; $\\mathbb B\\to2.5\\cdot10^6,7776$ | 2b (kept from the first pass, not extended) | hp 100-120 digits, relative $10^{-59}\\ldots10^{-45}$ |\n| $L=3$ table: six $[1,0,1]$ states reproduce the data | 2c | hp 70 digits, $10^{-41}$; 8 digits vs data |\n| exact untwisted singlets, pair data, $\\hat t_3=\\mp9/64$, $AC=4$, $K_1=10,2$ | 3.1, 3.2 | exact |\n| $A,B,C$ of the twisted chain $\\to(2,-12,2)$, $(-2,4,-2)$ | 3.2b | hp, $\\sim10^{-12}$ |\n| $\\nu y_{2,4}\\to\\mp\\tau/(4h^3)$, $y_2+y_4\\to-(\\tau+h\\tau')/(4h^4)$, $\\mathbb W\\to B_1^2$ on the singlets | 3.3 | analytic derivation; exact on the singlets; hp on the chain |\n| $\\mathbb W\\to B_1^2$ on all 28 zero-weight states | 3.3, last code cell | hp; deviation $3\\cdot10^{-3}$, $1.6\\cdot10^{-3}$ at $\\varepsilon=1/800,1/1600$, halving with $\\varepsilon$ |\n| parity shortcut $B_1=16\\tau^2-4\\tau-1+8x$ | 3.3 | exact on the singlets only; **fails** on the other states |\n\n**Open items.** (1) General-$L$ proof of the $B_z$ form (exact at $L=2,3$, model-exact at $L=4$) and a determinant/Pfaffian form for $B_z$ and $P_\\kappa$. (2) $\\tau_1'(\\theta_F)$ as a Q-expression (the parity shortcut removes it only on the singlets). (3) $L=3$: the individual factors are not separately finite ($\\mathbb W\\sim\\varepsilon^2$, $\\langle0\\vert\\Psi\\rangle/\\Vert\\Psi\\Vert\\sim\\varepsilon^{-3}$, $\\mathcal N_{\\rm pre}\\sim\\varepsilon$), so the untwisted-limit analysis of Part 3 must be redone with the combined scaling at $L\\ge3$; the $L=3$ norm is taken from the eigenvector. (4) Middle bridges $2\\le M\\le L-2$. (5) Finite-twist regularisation: with the Q-norm $C_Q(\\varepsilon)=C_{\\rm direct}(\\varepsilon)/\\sqrt H$, $H=1+O(\\varepsilon)$, and $K_\\kappa$ at $z_2\\ne z_3$ holds only in the limit; an exactly untwisted ($z_2=z_3$) companion-frame treatment is not available.",
